{% set r = (state_attr('sensor.camera_flap_rate','door_rolling') or {}) %}A door contact opened and the camera that covers that door did not report motion - repeatedly - including openings where other cameras did see activity.

{% for c in (state_attr('sensor.camera_flap_rate','door_coverage_failing') or []) %}{% set x = r.get(c) or {} %}- {{ c }}: saw {{ x.get('saw', 0) }} of {{ x.get('trips', 0) }} door trips in the last {{ x.get('days', 0) }} days ({{ x.get('missed', 0) }} corroborated misses, {{ x.get('unseen', 0) }} nobody saw); last saw its door {{ (x.get('last_saw') ~ 'Z') if x.get('last_saw') else 'not in that period' }}
{% endfor %}
Rule: at least 4 judged trips, no more than 20 % seen, at least 2 corroborated misses (openings where another camera did fire). Openings nobody saw are not misses, but they still count as trips the camera did not see. This does not depend on motion staleness: a camera that still fires now and then never goes stale. Check the camera's motion detection, zones, schedule, snooze and Modes in the Ring app, then walk-test the door. A miss is evidence, not proof - someone can leave by a door and walk out of view - so the count, not one event, is the signal. {{ now().strftime('%b %-d %-I:%M %p') }}.
